      "side": 1,
      "message": "This still looks agent-specific to me.\n\nI wonder whether `DynamicItem\u003cAiReviewProvider\u003e` is the right abstraction here, or whether this should become a `DynamicSet\u003cAiReviewProvider\u003e` instead.\n\nWith a set, Gerrit could expose multiple registered AI providers at the same time, rather than assuming there is only one active provider. That would also make the model list more natural: one agent could contribute several models (for example Gemini), while another agent could contribute a different set of models (for example Claude).\n\nThat seems like a better match for the generic provider design than keeping a single `DynamicItem`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 6,
